{
 "version": 1,
 "style": "B1",
 "width": 1280,
 "height": 720,
 "fps": 30,
 "voice": {
  "path": "narration.wav",
  "lead": 0.15,
  "tail": 5
 },
 "captions": [
  {
   "start": 0.15,
   "end": 1.35,
   "text": "You wake up at midnight,"
  },
  {
   "start": 1.71,
   "end": 2.45,
   "text": "look in the mirror,"
  },
  {
   "start": 2.67,
   "end": 4.47,
   "text": "and the voices in your head are gone."
  },
  {
   "start": 4.65,
   "end": 6.81,
   "text": "Instead, ticking silently on your"
  },
  {
   "start": 6.81,
   "end": 8.73,
   "text": "forehead is a luminous digital clock."
  },
  {
   "start": 8.73,
   "end": 10.29,
   "text": "Fifty-two years."
  },
  {
   "start": 10.29,
   "end": 12.35,
   "text": "One hundred and eighty-four days."
  },
  {
   "start": 12.35,
   "end": 13.51,
   "text": "Fourteen hours."
  },
  {
   "start": 13.77,
   "end": 15.53,
   "text": "And counting down with every heartbeat."
  },
  {
   "start": 16.03,
   "end": 17.09,
   "text": "You touch your brow."
  },
  {
   "start": 17.53,
   "end": 18.13,
   "text": "Cold skin."
  },
  {
   "start": 18.41,
   "end": 19.47,
   "text": "But the digits remain."
  },
  {
   "start": 19.97,
   "end": 21.45,
   "text": "You step out onto your balcony."
  },
  {
   "start": 21.85,
   "end": 24.15,
   "text": "A street cleaner is sweeping autumn leaves."
  },
  {
   "start": 24.15,
   "end": 25.15,
   "text": "Above his head:"
  },
  {
   "start": 25.43,
   "end": 27.07,
   "text": "four years, two months."
  },
  {
   "start": 27.39,
   "end": 28.99,
   "text": "A teenager laughs on a skateboard:"
  },
  {
   "start": 28.99,
   "end": 30.81,
   "text": "sixty-eight years."
  },
  {
   "start": 31.01,
   "end": 32.31,
   "text": "And then you see a young,"
  },
  {
   "start": 32.31,
   "end": 34.77,
   "text": "athletic jogger in neon running shoes."
  },
  {
   "start": 34.99,
   "end": 36.85,
   "text": "His clock is glowing dark red:"
  },
  {
   "start": 36.99,
   "end": 37.91,
   "text": "Zero years."
  },
  {
   "start": 38.25,
   "end": 39.07,
   "text": "Zero days."
  },
  {
   "start": 39.45,
   "end": 40.99,
   "text": "One hour and fourteen minutes."
  },
  {
   "start": 41.33,
   "end": 42.83,
   "text": "For the next seven days,"
  },
  {
   "start": 42.99,
   "end": 44.87,
   "text": "you can see the exact expiration"
  },
  {
   "start": 44.87,
   "end": 46.93,
   "text": "date of every human soul on earth."
  },
  {
   "start": 47.09,
   "end": 48.27,
   "text": "And by day seven,"
  },
  {
   "start": 48.39,
   "end": 50.83,
   "text": "you will realize that humans don't fear dying."
  },
  {
   "start": 50.83,
   "end": 53.49,
   "text": "We fear realizing how much of life we threw"
  },
  {
   "start": 53.49,
   "end": 55.37,
   "text": "away while pretending we were immortal."
  },
  {
   "start": 55.71,
   "end": 58.37,
   "text": "At first, your instinct is sheer panic."
  },
  {
   "start": 58.55,
   "end": 61.25,
   "text": "Because you realize that every room you enter is filled"
  },
  {
   "start": 61.25,
   "end": 64.09,
   "text": "with people walking toward invisible trapdoors."
  },
  {
   "start": 64.09,
   "end": 65.43,
   "text": "At the subway station,"
  },
  {
   "start": 65.63,
   "end": 67.47,
   "text": "hundreds of numbers bob in unison."
  },
  {
   "start": 67.47,
   "end": 68.73,
   "text": "Thirty years."
  },
  {
   "start": 68.73,
   "end": 69.97,
   "text": "Fifty years."
  },
  {
   "start": 69.97,
   "end": 71.19,
   "text": "Twelve years."
  },
  {
   "start": 71.43,
   "end": 72.85,
   "text": "And you notice something bizarre:"
  },
  {
   "start": 73.23,
   "end": 75.53,
   "text": "The people with fifty or sixty years on their"
  },
  {
   "start": 75.53,
   "end": 77.21,
   "text": "clocks are the ones looking miserable."
  },
  {
   "start": 77.21,
   "end": 79.37,
   "text": "They sit with slouched shoulders,"
  },
  {
   "start": 79.37,
   "end": 81.39,
   "text": "doom-scrolling short videos,"
  },
  {
   "start": 81.77,
   "end": 83.93,
   "text": "staring into screens with vacant eyes."
  },
  {
   "start": 84.17,
   "end": 85.49,
   "text": "They take out their phones,"
  },
  {
   "start": 85.93,
   "end": 86.71,
   "text": "ignore their children,"
  },
  {
   "start": 87.07,
   "end": 88.65,
   "text": "and snap at the ticket vendor."
  },
  {
   "start": 89.01,
   "end": 89.29,
   "text": "Why?"
  },
  {
   "start": 89.59,
   "end": 90.97,
   "text": "Because when your clock says"
  },
  {
   "start": 90.97,
   "end": 92.55,
   "text": "you have fifty years left,"
  },
  {
   "start": 92.79,
   "end": 95.29,
   "text": "each individual hour feels essentially worthless."
  },
  {
   "start": 95.65,
   "end": 97.87,
   "text": "You treat time like Monopoly money because"
  },
  {
   "start": 97.87,
   "end": 99.59,
   "text": "you assume the bank never closes."
  },
  {
   "start": 100.19,
   "end": 102.11,
   "text": "Roman philosopher Seneca wrote about"
  },
  {
   "start": 102.11,
   "end": 103.83,
   "text": "this two thousand years ago:"
  },
  {
   "start": 103.83,
   "end": 106.19,
   "text": "You live as if you are destined to live forever."
  },
  {
   "start": 106.51,
   "end": 108.99,
   "text": "No thought of your frailty ever enters your head."
  },
  {
   "start": 109.01,
   "end": 110.33,
   "text": "When death feels distant,"
  },
  {
   "start": 110.81,
   "end": 111.75,
   "text": "life feels cheap."
  },
  {
   "start": 112.348,
   "end": 113.548,
   "text": "On day two,"
  },
  {
   "start": 113.848,
   "end": 115.708,
   "text": "you can't stop thinking about the jogger."
  },
  {
   "start": 115.708,
   "end": 117.128,
   "text": "The neon shoes."
  },
  {
   "start": 117.628,
   "end": 119.208,
   "text": "The one hour and fourteen minutes."
  },
  {
   "start": 119.928,
   "end": 120.988,
   "text": "You check local news."
  },
  {
   "start": 121.448,
   "end": 123.028,
   "text": "At one fifteen yesterday morning,"
  },
  {
   "start": 123.348,
   "end": 125.728,
   "text": "a delivery truck ran a light three blocks away."
  },
  {
   "start": 126.388,
   "end": 127.528,
   "text": "A jogger was struck."
  },
  {
   "start": 128.388,
   "end": 129.628,
   "text": "The clock wasn't a probability."
  },
  {
   "start": 129.908,
   "end": 130.688,
   "text": "It wasn't a warning."
  },
  {
   "start": 131.488,
   "end": 132.588,
   "text": "It was a fact."
  },
  {
   "start": 133.508,
   "end": 134.408,
   "text": "By day three,"
  },
  {
   "start": 134.768,
   "end": 136.788,
   "text": "the knowledge becomes an unbearable weight."
  },
  {
   "start": 137.208,
   "end": 138.348,
   "text": "You walk into your office."
  },
  {
   "start": 138.808,
   "end": 140.428,
   "text": "Kevin's clock says forty-one years."
  },
  {
   "start": 140.428,
   "end": 142.668,
   "text": "Your manager's clock says twenty-eight years."
  },
  {
   "start": 143.208,
   "end": 145.048,
   "text": "Then an elderly courier delivers a"
  },
  {
   "start": 145.048,
   "end": 146.408,
   "text": "package to the reception desk."
  },
  {
   "start": 147.068,
   "end": 148.768,
   "text": "His timer: two days,"
  },
  {
   "start": 149.008,
   "end": 149.648,
   "text": "three hours."
  },
  {
   "start": 149.648,
   "end": 151.148,
   "text": "He is laughing,"
  },
  {
   "start": 151.548,
   "end": 153.088,
   "text": "telling a joke to the receptionist,"
  },
  {
   "start": 153.088,
   "end": 155.688,
   "text": "entirely unaware that forty-eight hours from now,"
  },
  {
   "start": 155.768,
   "end": 157.488,
   "text": "his story on earth is finished."
  },
  {
   "start": 158.168,
   "end": 158.688,
   "text": "You freeze."
  },
  {
   "start": 159.348,
   "end": 160.028,
   "text": "Do you tell him?"
  },
  {
   "start": 160.308,
   "end": 160.988,
   "text": "Excuse me, sir."
  },
  {
   "start": 161.128,
   "end": 161.668,
   "text": "Go home."
  },
  {
   "start": 161.908,
   "end": 162.508,
   "text": "Call your daughter."
  },
  {
   "start": 162.748,
   "end": 163.508,
   "text": "Cancel your shifts."
  },
  {
   "start": 164.048,
   "end": 164.808,
   "text": "What would he say?"
  },
  {
   "start": 165.188,
   "end": 166.108,
   "text": "He'd think you're insane."
  },
  {
   "start": 166.368,
   "end": 167.588,
   "text": "He'd call building security."
  },
  {
   "start": 168.548,
   "end": 171.148,
   "text": "Psychologists call this Terror Management Theory:"
  },
  {
   "start": 171.448,
   "end": 173.948,
   "text": "humans maintain elaborate cultural systems"
  },
  {
   "start": 173.948,
   "end": 176.208,
   "text": "and daily routines specifically to suppress"
  },
  {
   "start": 176.208,
   "end": 178.468,
   "text": "the terrifying awareness of our mortality."
  },
  {
   "start": 179.088,
   "end": 181.228,
   "text": "If you tear away that veil without warning,"
  },
  {
   "start": 181.708,
   "end": 182.928,
   "text": "you don't liberate someone."
  },
  {
   "start": 183.208,
   "end": 184.948,
   "text": "You induce psychological collapse."
  },
  {
   "start": 185.588,
   "end": 187.768,
   "text": "You realize the horror of omniscience:"
  },
  {
   "start": 188.328,
   "end": 190.648,
   "text": "knowing the future doesn't give you control over it."
  },
  {
   "start": 190.748,
   "end": 193.428,
   "text": "It only forces you to grieve before the loss happens."
  },
  {
   "start": 194.088,
   "end": 195.188,
   "text": "On day four,"
  },
  {
   "start": 195.568,
   "end": 196.748,
   "text": "you refuse to be passive."
  },
  {
   "start": 197.308,
   "end": 198.808,
   "text": "You decide you're going to break the rule."
  },
  {
   "start": 199.588,
   "end": 200.468,
   "text": "At the city library,"
  },
  {
   "start": 200.628,
   "end": 203.008,
   "text": "a college student is studying alone at a wooden desk."
  },
  {
   "start": 203.428,
   "end": 205.248,
   "text": "Her timer: thirty-five minutes."
  },
  {
   "start": 205.768,
   "end": 207.228,
   "text": "You sit two tables away,"
  },
  {
   "start": 207.628,
   "end": 208.508,
   "text": "watching the seconds melt."
  },
  {
   "start": 209.088,
   "end": 210.188,
   "text": "At ten minutes left,"
  },
  {
   "start": 210.388,
   "end": 212.448,
   "text": "she packs her laptop into her canvas bag,"
  },
  {
   "start": 212.828,
   "end": 214.648,
   "text": "stands up, and walks toward the exit."
  },
  {
   "start": 215.168,
   "end": 215.908,
   "text": "You follow her."
  },
  {
   "start": 216.288,
   "end": 217.648,
   "text": "She steps onto the crosswalk."
  },
  {
   "start": 218.028,
   "end": 220.088,
   "text": "A city bus turns the corner fast,"
  },
  {
   "start": 220.348,
   "end": 221.508,
   "text": "blinding rain on the windshield."
  },
  {
   "start": 221.508,
   "end": 222.628,
   "text": "You don't think."
  },
  {
   "start": 222.628,
   "end": 223.608,
   "text": "You sprint forward,"
  },
  {
   "start": 223.748,
   "end": 224.408,
   "text": "grab her backpack,"
  },
  {
   "start": 224.768,
   "end": 226.268,
   "text": "and yank her backward onto the sidewalk."
  },
  {
   "start": 226.788,
   "end": 228.108,
   "text": "The bus roars past,"
  },
  {
   "start": 228.108,
   "end": 229.908,
   "text": "spraying puddle water across her jeans."
  },
  {
   "start": 230.328,
   "end": 231.548,
   "text": "She stumbles, gasping,"
  },
  {
   "start": 231.628,
   "end": 232.668,
   "text": "furious and terrified:"
  },
  {
   "start": 232.868,
   "end": 233.748,
   "text": "What is wrong with you?!"
  },
  {
   "start": 233.888,
   "end": 234.628,
   "text": "Let go of me!"
  },
  {
   "start": 235.308,
   "end": 236.208,
   "text": "You look at her forehead."
  },
  {
   "start": 236.828,
   "end": 238.728,
   "text": "The timer didn't reset to eighty years."
  },
  {
   "start": 239.168,
   "end": 239.888,
   "text": "It didn't disappear."
  },
  {
   "start": 240.528,
   "end": 242.908,
   "text": "The digits simply shifted by sixteen minutes:"
  },
  {
   "start": 243.568,
   "end": 244.248,
   "text": "Zero hours."
  },
  {
   "start": 244.248,
   "end": 245.348,
   "text": "Sixteen minutes."
  },
  {
   "start": 245.348,
   "end": 246.568,
   "text": "Twenty-eight seconds."
  },
  {
   "start": 247.048,
   "end": 248.728,
   "text": "Your stomach drops into ice water."
  },
  {
   "start": 249.228,
   "end": 250.548,
   "text": "You didn't cure mortality."
  },
  {
   "start": 250.868,
   "end": 252.528,
   "text": "You merely postponed the collision."
  },
  {
   "start": 253.228,
   "end": 255.668,
   "text": "Death wasn't a specific bus on a specific street."
  },
  {
   "start": 255.948,
   "end": 258.608,
   "text": "It was an inevitable biological and physical"
  },
  {
   "start": 258.608,
   "end": 261.028,
   "text": "certainty woven into the fabric of time."
  },
  {
   "start": 261.468,
   "end": 262.348,
   "text": "By day five,"
  },
  {
   "start": 262.528,
   "end": 264.588,
   "text": "after shadowing her and watching her collapse"
  },
  {
   "start": 264.588,
   "end": 266.908,
   "text": "from an undiagnosed aneurysm in a pharmacy,"
  },
  {
   "start": 267.448,
   "end": 269.908,
   "text": "you understand: You cannot cheat the ledger."
  },
  {
   "start": 270.328,
   "end": 272.808,
   "text": "You can only torture yourself trying to outrun it."
  },
  {
   "start": 273.388,
   "end": 274.508,
   "text": "On day six,"
  },
  {
   "start": 274.848,
   "end": 276.068,
   "text": "you stop looking at strangers."
  },
  {
   "start": 276.788,
   "end": 278.028,
   "text": "You take the train home."
  },
  {
   "start": 278.768,
   "end": 280.788,
   "text": "You open the front door of your childhood house."
  },
  {
   "start": 281.428,
   "end": 283.468,
   "text": "The smell of cinnamon and roasted tea."
  },
  {
   "start": 284.008,
   "end": 286.188,
   "text": "Your mother turns from the stove with a warm smile."
  },
  {
   "start": 286.868,
   "end": 288.648,
   "text": "Your father looks up from his crossword puzzle."
  },
  {
   "start": 289.428,
   "end": 290.948,
   "text": "And before you can stop yourself,"
  },
  {
   "start": 291.548,
   "end": 293.008,
   "text": "your eyes flick upward."
  },
  {
   "start": 293.768,
   "end": 295.408,
   "text": "Mother: seven years,"
  },
  {
   "start": 295.628,
   "end": 296.168,
   "text": "four months."
  },
  {
   "start": 296.888,
   "end": 298.708,
   "text": "Father: three years,"
  },
  {
   "start": 298.908,
   "end": 299.508,
   "text": "eight months."
  },
  {
   "start": 300.328,
   "end": 302.688,
   "text": "A physical blow strikes your chest."
  },
  {
   "start": 303.348,
   "end": 305.708,
   "text": "You've always known intellectually that"
  },
  {
   "start": 305.708,
   "end": 307.228,
   "text": "your parents wouldn't live forever."
  },
  {
   "start": 307.648,
   "end": 308.868,
   "text": "Every human knows this."
  },
  {
   "start": 309.228,
   "end": 310.568,
   "text": "Yet we postpone visits."
  },
  {
   "start": 311.228,
   "end": 312.968,
   "text": "We answer their phone calls with rushed,"
  },
  {
   "start": 313.168,
   "end": 314.068,
   "text": "distracted voices."
  },
  {
   "start": 314.588,
   "end": 315.368,
   "text": "We tell ourselves:"
  },
  {
   "start": 315.528,
   "end": 316.668,
   "text": "I'll visit next weekend."
  },
  {
   "start": 317.108,
   "end": 318.408,
   "text": "I'll take them to dinner next month."
  },
  {
   "start": 318.408,
   "end": 319.768,
   "text": "When work calms down."
  },
  {
   "start": 320.568,
   "end": 321.668,
   "text": "Standing in that kitchen,"
  },
  {
   "start": 322.068,
   "end": 324.408,
   "text": "looking at three years and eight months,"
  },
  {
   "start": 324.988,
   "end": 327.988,
   "text": "the arithmetic of your entire life rewrites itself."
  },
  {
   "start": 328.668,
   "end": 330.188,
   "text": "If you visit twice a year,"
  },
  {
   "start": 330.628,
   "end": 332.048,
   "text": "three years means you will see"
  },
  {
   "start": 332.048,
   "end": 334.168,
   "text": "your father six more times."
  },
  {
   "start": 334.708,
   "end": 335.428,
   "text": "Not hundreds."
  },
  {
   "start": 336.268,
   "end": 336.628,
   "text": "Six."
  },
  {
   "start": 337.408,
   "end": 338.508,
   "text": "For the rest of the evening,"
  },
  {
   "start": 338.908,
   "end": 340.208,
   "text": "you don't check your phone once."
  },
  {
   "start": 340.788,
   "end": 342.148,
   "text": "You ask your father about his"
  },
  {
   "start": 342.148,
   "end": 343.388,
   "text": "childhood in the countryside."
  },
  {
   "start": 343.948,
   "end": 346.168,
   "text": "You listen to every single detail"
  },
  {
   "start": 346.168,
   "end": 347.108,
   "text": "of your mother's recipe."
  },
  {
   "start": 347.688,
   "end": 349.308,
   "text": "You hold their hands when you leave."
  },
  {
   "start": 350.028,
   "end": 351.608,
   "text": "And for the first time in your life,"
  },
  {
   "start": 352.008,
   "end": 354.288,
   "text": "you aren't living in the phantom future."
  },
  {
   "start": 354.288,
   "end": 355.808,
   "text": "You are fully,"
  },
  {
   "start": 356.488,
   "end": 359.548,
   "text": "acutely, painfully alive in the present."
  },
  {
   "start": 360.368,
   "end": 361.588,
   "text": "Day seven arrives."
  },
  {
   "start": 362.188,
   "end": 362.968,
   "text": "Midnight approaches."
  },
  {
   "start": 363.648,
   "end": 365.928,
   "text": "You stand before the mirror in your dark apartment."
  },
  {
   "start": 366.708,
   "end": 368.428,
   "text": "Your own forehead is ticking down."
  },
  {
   "start": 368.428,
   "end": 369.908,
   "text": "Fifty-two years."
  },
  {
   "start": 370.608,
   "end": 371.468,
   "text": "You look at the numbers,"
  },
  {
   "start": 372.128,
   "end": 373.108,
   "text": "and the fear is gone."
  },
  {
   "start": 373.888,
   "end": 377.108,
   "text": "Instead, a profound reverence fills the room."
  },
  {
   "start": 377.748,
   "end": 379.148,
   "text": "If human life were infinite,"
  },
  {
   "start": 379.808,
   "end": 381.908,
   "text": "no decision would ever carry weight."
  },
  {
   "start": 382.288,
   "end": 384.548,
   "text": "You could learn guitar in five hundred years."
  },
  {
   "start": 384.588,
   "end": 386.348,
   "text": "You could apologize in three centuries."
  },
  {
   "start": 389.708,
   "end": 390.348,
   "text": "You could forgive someone tomorrow,"
  },
  {
   "start": 390.348,
   "end": 390.398,
   "text": "or in a millennium."
  },
  {
   "start": 390.398,
   "end": 391.908,
   "text": "Because nothing would ever be lost."
  },
  {
   "start": 392.568,
   "end": 394.648,
   "text": "A painting is only beautiful because"
  },
  {
   "start": 394.648,
   "end": 396.528,
   "text": "of the frame that encloses it."
  },
  {
   "start": 396.768,
   "end": 398.448,
   "text": "Music is only heartbreaking because"
  },
  {
   "start": 398.448,
   "end": 400.388,
   "text": "the chord must eventually end."
  },
  {
   "start": 401.188,
   "end": 404.848,
   "text": "And love only burns with divine intensity because"
  },
  {
   "start": 404.848,
   "end": 407.408,
   "text": "the people we love can be taken from us."
  },
  {
   "start": 408.008,
   "end": 409.458,
   "text": "The digital clock reaches eleven"
  },
  {
   "start": 409.458,
   "end": 411.148,
   "text": "fifty-nine and fifty seconds."
  },
  {
   "start": 411.148,
   "end": 412.568,
   "text": "Ten seconds."
  },
  {
   "start": 412.928,
   "end": 413.528,
   "text": "Five."
  },
  {
   "start": 414.208,
   "end": 414.688,
   "text": "Four."
  },
  {
   "start": 415.328,
   "end": 415.728,
   "text": "Three."
  },
  {
   "start": 416.468,
   "end": 416.708,
   "text": "Two."
  },
  {
   "start": 417.408,
   "end": 417.808,
   "text": "One."
  },
  {
   "start": 417.808,
   "end": 420.668,
   "text": "The glowing blue digits dissolve into thin air."
  },
  {
   "start": 421.248,
   "end": 422.588,
   "text": "Your reflection looks back at you."
  },
  {
   "start": 423.208,
   "end": 423.768,
   "text": "Smooth brow."
  },
  {
   "start": 424.488,
   "end": 424.908,
   "text": "No countdown."
  },
  {
   "start": 425.788,
   "end": 426.268,
   "text": "No spoilers."
  },
  {
   "start": 426.968,
   "end": 428.848,
   "text": "You don't know if you have fifty years left,"
  },
  {
   "start": 428.848,
   "end": 431.048,
   "text": "fifty days, or fifty minutes."
  },
  {
   "start": 431.488,
   "end": 433.288,
   "text": "And that is the greatest gift"
  },
  {
   "start": 433.288,
   "end": 434.468,
   "text": "the universe ever gave you."
  },
  {
   "start": 434.988,
   "end": 437.208,
   "text": "Because the only day that ever matters is"
  },
  {
   "start": 437.208,
   "end": 438.928,
   "text": "the one you are standing in right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 439.568,
   "end": 441.328,
   "text": "Tomorrow, the countdown disappears."
  },
  {
   "start": 442.348,
   "end": 443.288,
   "text": "Until you meet someone,"
  },
  {
   "start": 443.848,
   "end": 444.728,
   "text": "look into their eyes,"
  },
  {
   "start": 445.328,
   "end": 447.068,
   "text": "and see a word floating above their"
  },
  {
   "start": 447.068,
   "end": 448.208,
   "text": "lips every time they speak."
  },
  {
   "start": 448.908,
   "end": 451.408,
   "text": "What if you could see every single lie?"
  },
  {
   "start": 452.528,
   "end": 453.008,
   "text": "Subscribe."
  },
  {
   "start": 453.008,
   "end": 455.448,
   "text": "Because tomorrow, the truth comes out."
  }
